    "finalMessage": "The film is built, but I could not open it in a real browser from this session, so the actual WebGL render and the \"no console errors\" rule are still unconfirmed.\n\nWhat I did check, in Node with Three.js 0.170.0 loaded from the CDN:\n- **Full timeline:** all 30 seconds stepped at 60 fps with no exceptions, no console output and no invalid transforms.\n- **Loop:** the camera pose at 0 s and 30 s is identical, and the book is closed again at both ends.\n- **Composition:** I looked at software-rendered preview frames (flat colour, no shadows) at 18 timestamps. The book, the page turns and all four worlds appear and are framed at 16:9.\n\nNot checked: shadows, lighting levels, and the page code in `index.html` and `src/main.js`, which only run in a browser.\n\nKnown rough edges:\n- In the jungle, a few foreground fern blades overhang the page edge by up to about 0.3 units. The worker assigned to fix this ran out of steps after lowering the palm crowns, and I left the overhang.\n- The turning page is a rigid sheet with no bend.\n\n## Files\n- `index.html` \u2014 entry point with the import map\n- `src/main.js` \u2014 renderer, lights, table, play loop, `?t=` handling\n- `src/timeline.js` \u2014 the 30-second schedule (cover, page turns, pop-ups)\n- `src/camera.js` \u2014 camera path\n- `src/book.js` \u2014 book, cover and turning pages\n- `src/paper.js` \u2014 shared paper card and pop-up hinge helpers\n- `src/worlds/castle.js`\n- `src/worlds/jungle.js`\n- `src/worlds/port.js`\n- `src/worlds/peaks.js`\n\n## How to view\nFrom this folder, start any static file server, for example:\n\n```\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/index.html`. It plays automatically at full window size and loops. Add `?t=12.5` (any number of seconds) to jump to that time and freeze there for a screenshot.\n\nTiming, for picking screenshot times: the castle is up from about 4.4 to 8.3 s, the jungle 11.3 to 14.5 s, the port 17.5 to 20.7 s, the peaks 23.7 to 26.9 s, and the book closes between 27.7 and 29.5 s."
